# Manual tour of the sample API.
# Start it first:  dotnet run --project samples/Keel.Sample
# Open this file in Visual Studio, Rider or VS Code (REST Client extension) and send each request.

@host = http://localhost:55797

### 1. Public endpoint ([AllowAnonymous]) -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/health

### 2. Protected endpoint without credentials -> 401 (group-level RequireAuthorization)
GET {{host}}/api/invoices

### 3. Create an invoice (contract read from the body) -> 201
POST {{host}}/api/invoices
X-Api-Key: demo
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customer": "Acme", "amount": 120 }

### 4. Invalid contract -> 400 problem details from .NET 10 validation
POST {{host}}/api/invoices
X-Api-Key: demo
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customer": "", "amount": 0 }

### 5. Get by id (route binding, Results<Ok, NotFound>) -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/invoices/inv-1
X-Api-Key: demo

### 6. Unknown id -> 404
GET {{host}}/api/invoices/nope
X-Api-Key: demo

### 7. List with a query filter -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/invoices?status=open
X-Api-Key: demo

### 8. Route value + validated [FromBody] member -> 204
PUT {{host}}/api/invoices/inv-1/customer
X-Api-Key: demo
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customer": "Globex" }

### 9. Delete as a normal user -> 403 (policy "admin" set in Configure)
DELETE {{host}}/api/invoices/inv-1
X-Api-Key: demo

### 10. Delete as admin -> 204
DELETE {{host}}/api/invoices/inv-1
X-Api-Key: admin

### 11. Server-Sent Events stream
GET {{host}}/api/invoices/events?count=3
X-Api-Key: demo
